Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here’s how you could write an “if/then” statement in C:

if (condition1) {
  // do something
}

if (condition2) {
  // do something else
}

You can also put multiple conditions into a single if statement:

if (condition1 && condition2) {
  // do something
}

where “condition1” and “condition2” can be any number of expressions that evaluate to either a boolean value of TRUE or FALSE.

